.{
    // A007 is a rule aegis declares (its lint_rules, read from the pinned aegis): a reference to one
    // of its targets (std's locks, atomics and futex calls) reached through each way a name is held,
    // and the same way reaching aegis's guarded types.
    // A target is a declaration, reached only by a name evaluated as the program compiles; memory
    // a load or store moves holds runtime values, never a name.
    .na = .{.memory},
}
